{"analytics_identifier":null,"base_path":"/free-school-transport","content_id":"fdd55911-6fcc-4b9e-be9f-34e93298b691","description":"Free transport from your local council - eligibility, rules for children with special educational needs and disabilities (SEND), how to apply","details":{"body":"<p>Children of <a href=\"/schools-admissions/school-starting-age\">compulsory school age</a> qualify for free school transport if they go to their nearest suitable school and any of the following apply:</p>\n\n<ul>\n  <li>the school is more than 2 miles away and the child is under 8</li>\n  <li>the school is more than 3 miles away and the child is 8 or over</li>\n  <li>there’s no safe walking route between their home and school</li>\n  <li>they cannot walk there because of their <a href=\"/apply-school-transport-for-child-with-special-educational-needs-sen\">special educational needs or disabilities or a mobility problem</a>\n</li>\n</ul>\n\n<div role=\"note\" aria-label=\"Information\" class=\"application-notice info-notice\">\n  <p>If your child is 16 or over and still in education, <a href=\"/subsidised-college-transport-16-19\">ask your local council</a> if they offer any help with transport.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h2 id=\"if-your-child-is-eligible-for-free-school-meals\">If your child is eligible for free school meals</h2>\n\n<p>Your child may also qualify for free school transport if they’re eligible for free school meals. They may be eligible for free school meals if you get certain benefits.</p>\n\n<p><a href=\"/apply-free-school-meals\">Check if your child is eligible for free school meals</a>.</p>\n\n<p>From the start of the 2026 to 2027 academic year, your child will continue to be eligible for free school transport if you get Universal Credit and have a household income of £7,400 or less a year (after tax and not including any benefits you get).</p>\n\n<p>Your child must also be:</p>\n\n<ul>\n  <li>aged 8 to 11, go to their nearest school and it’s at least 2 miles away</li>\n  <li>aged 11 to 16 and go to a school 2 to 6 miles away - if it’s one of their 3 nearest suitable schools</li>\n  <li>aged 11 to 16 and go to a school 2 to 15 miles away - if it’s one you chose because of your religion or belief</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h2 id=\"how-to-apply\">How to apply</h2>\n\n<p>Find out more about <a href=\"/help-home-school-transport\">applying for free school transport</a> from your local council.</p>\n","external_related_links":[]},"document_type":"answer","first_published_at":"2012-10-16T10:28:33+01:00","links":{"available_translations":[{"api_path":"/api/content/free-school-transport","api_url":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/free-school-transport","base_path":"/free-school-transport","content_id":"fdd55911-6fcc-4b9e-be9f-34e93298b691","document_type":"answer","links":{},"locale":"en","public_updated_at":"2016-06-24T09:05:23Z","schema_name":"answer","title":"Free school transport","web_url":"https://www.gov.uk/free-school-transport","withdrawn":false}],"mainstream_browse_pages":[{"api_path":"/api/content/browse/childcare-parenting/financial-help-children","api_url":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/browse/childcare-parenting/financial-help-children","base_path":"/browse/childcare-parenting/financial-help-children","content_id":"e027612d-17f3-4183-ae8d-cde8f43dc471","description":"Includes help when having a baby or adopting, child benefit and tax credits, support for childcare","document_type":"mainstream_browse_page","links":{},"locale":"en","public_updated_at":"2025-04-06T20:12:50Z","schema_name":"mainstream_browse_page","title":"Financial help if you have children","web_url":"https://www.gov.uk/browse/childcare-parenting/financial-help-children","withdrawn":false},{"api_path":"/api/content/browse/childcare-parenting/schools-education","api_url":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/browse/childcare-parenting/schools-education","base_path":"/browse/childcare-parenting/schools-education","content_id":"6e3014fa-5bd1-48b9-9aab-f7b1241afdb6","descriptio